---- Content licensing ------------------------------------------------------

The Apache-2.0 terms above cover the ENGINE — the C sources, the tooling, and
the tests. Content shipped with or contributed to a game built on it is
licensed separately, because Apache-2.0 is a software licence and Creative
Commons themselves advise against applying CC licences to code:

  - Assets (graphics, audio) must be contributed under CC0 or CC BY 4.0.
    CC BY-NC and CC BY-ND are NOT acceptable: NonCommercial forbids sale on
    Steam, the console stores and the App Store, and NoDerivatives forbids the
    modification a remix community exists to do. One of either, accepted early
    and forgotten, is removed rather than relicensed.
  - Fonts: SIL Open Font License, or none. The §12 presentation interface
    freezes text as METRICS rather than glyphs, so a backend may supply its own
    rather than the project bundling one.

Every contributed asset carries a manifest entry naming its author, licence
and source. That entry is the record for both obligations at once: CC BY
attribution, and the credits.

